# 1. The Physical Internet / How the Internet Works
# Internet kya hai?
Internet duniya bhar ke computers aur networks ka ek bahut bada network hai jo TCP/IP protocol ke through ek dusre se communicate karta hai.

Simple Definition
Internet ek global network of networks hai jo duniya ke lakho-crodo devices ko connect karta hai aur information share karne ki suvidha deta hai.

Features
Worldwide connectivity provide karta hai.
Information sharing ko easy banata hai.
Email, web browsing, file transfer, video calling jaise services provide karta hai.
TCP/IP protocol par kaam karta hai.
24×7 available rehta hai.

Uses of Internet
Email bhejna aur receive karna
Web browsing
Online shopping
Online banking
Social media
Video conferencing
Online education

Example
Jab aap browser me koi website open karte hain, jaise Google, to Internet ke madhyam se aapka computer us website ke server se connect hota hai aur webpage display karta hai.

Exam Definition
"Internet is a worldwide network of interconnected computers and networks that communicate using TCP/IP protocols to share information and resources."

# Data ek device se doosre device tak kaise jata hai?
 Jab aap kisi device se data bhejte hain (jaise WhatsApp message, email, ya website request), to data kai steps se hokar destination device tak pahunchta hai.

Step 1: Data Create Hota Hai
User message ya file send karta hai.
Device data ko digital form (0 aur 1) me convert karta hai.

Step 2: Data Packets Me Divide Hota Hai
Bada data chhote-chhote packets me divide kiya jata hai.
Har packet me source address aur destination address hota hai.

Step 3: Router/Switch Tak Jata Hai
Packet pehle local network ke Switch ya Router tak pahunchta hai.
Router packet ke liye best path choose karta hai.

Step 4: Internet Ke Through Travel Karta Hai
Packets alag-alag networks aur routers se hokar travel karte hain.
Har router packet ko next destination ki taraf forward karta hai.

Step 5: Destination Device Tak Pahunchta Hai
Saare packets destination device par receive hote hain.
Device packets ko sahi order me jodkar original data bana deta hai.

> Example
Aap Chennai se apne dost ko Delhi me WhatsApp message "Hello" bhejte ho:
1 Message packet me convert hota hai.
2 Router aur Internet ke through travel karta hai.
3 Dost ke mobile tak pahunchta hai.
4 Mobile packets ko jodkar "Hello" display karta hai.

> Flow Diagram
Sender Device
      ↓
 Switch/Router
      ↓
   Internet
      ↓
 Routers
      ↓
Destination Device

> Exam Definition
"Data is transmitted from one device to another by dividing it into packets, routing those packets through network devices and the Internet, and reassembling them at the destination device."

# Routers, switches, cables, fiber optics ka role.
1. Switch
 Switch ek network device hai jo multiple devices ko LAN (Local Area Network) me connect karta hai.
Data ko sirf usi device tak bhejta hai jiske liye data hota hai.
MAC Address ka use karta hai.
Example:
College lab me 20 computers ko connect karne ke liye switch use kiya jata hai.

2. Router
 Router different networks ko connect karta hai.
Data packet ke liye best path select karta hai.
Internet access provide karta hai.
IP Address ka use karta hai.
Example:
Ghar ka Wi-Fi router aapke mobile aur laptop ko Internet se connect karta hai.

3. Cables
 Cables data ko ek device se doosre device tak physical medium ke through transfer karte hain.
Types:
Twisted Pair Cable (UTP)
Coaxial Cable
Example:
Computer ko switch se connect karne ke liye Ethernet cable use hoti hai.

4. Fiber Optics
 Fiber optic cable data ko light signals ke form me transfer karti hai.
Bahut high speed aur long-distance communication provide karti hai.
Signal loss bahut kam hota hai.

Example:
Internet Service Providers (ISP) high-speed broadband ke liye fiber optic cables use karte hain.


##  IP packets ka basic flow.
 IP Packet data ka ek chhota unit hota hai jo network ya Internet par travel karta hai. Har packet me Source IP Address aur Destination IP Address hota hai.

Basic Flow
Step 1: Data Create Hota Hai
User message, email, ya website request bhejta hai.
Data packets me divide ho jata hai.


Step 2: IP Address Add Hota Hai
Har packet me:
-Source IP (sender ka address)
-Destination IP (receiver ka address)
add kiya jata hai.

Step 3: Packet Router Tak Jata Hai
Packet local router ko milta hai.
Router destination IP check karta hai.

Step 4: Router Best Path Choose Karta Hai
Router routing table ka use karke next route decide karta hai.
Packet ek router se dusre router tak travel karta hai.

Step 5: Destination Network Tak Pahunchta Hai
Packet destination network ke router tak pahunchta hai.
Router packet ko correct device tak forward karta hai.

Step 6: Data Reassemble Hota Hai
Destination device saare packets receive karti hai.
Packets ko original order me jodkar complete data bana diya jata hai.

Example
Aap Chennai se Delhi me friend ko "Hello" bhejte ho:

Mobile
   ↓
Wi-Fi Router
   ↓
ISP Network
   ↓
Internet Routers
   ↓
Destination ISP
   ↓
Friend's Mobile

Message packet ban kar Internet ke routers se travel karta hai aur destination par pahunchkar phir se original message ban jata hai.

Simple Diagram
Sender
  ↓
Router
  ↓
Internet
  ↓
Router
  ↓
Receiver

Exam Definition
"An IP packet is a unit of data containing source and destination IP addresses that travels through routers across networks to reach its destination."



